# Non-secret deploy-time tuning knobs for the HOSTED agent.
#
# Tracked in git (unlike the developer .env, which holds real credentials and
# is gitignored). scripts/build_agent.sh copies this file to `.env` inside
# the zip staging directory — never the developer's own .env — and it still
# passes through the same credential scanner as everything else before the
# zip is written.
#
# MIN_CONFIDENCE: submission-gate confidence floor (main.py
# build_submission_policy). The solver's non-tool-exact answers carry a flat
# 0.7 confidence (solver/agent_loop.py _build_candidate); verification.py
# only ever LOWERS that value, never raises it. At the prior 0.80 default,
# every one of those answers was silently discarded forever — LOW_CONFIDENCE
# -> REJECTED -> terminal FAILED state, no retry (orchestrator/state.py:
# TileState.FAILED has no outgoing transitions). That meant every 200-500
# point tile outside a tool's exact_value path was structurally unsubmittable
# regardless of whether the answer was right.
#
# 0.70 is not an arbitrary loosening: it exactly matches the solver's normal
# verified-answer confidence, so a correct, non-flagged answer now clears the
# gate, while verification's own down-clamps (<=0.5 for no evidence, <=0.4
# for a failed check) still block anything it actually flagged as suspect.
#
# This is a stopgap. The permanent fix belongs in main.py (lower the
# default there) and ideally in orchestrator/board_loop.py (retry
# LOW_CONFIDENCE instead of permanently failing it) — see PR description.
export MIN_CONFIDENCE=0.70
